<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cleopatra VII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 51–30 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cleopatra VII was the last active ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a>, reigning from 51 to 30 BCE. She allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> in an attempt to preserve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s independence. After their defeat by Octavian at Actium, she died by suicide, and Egypt became a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii.jpg" alt="Cleopatra VII" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis le Grand · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kleopatra-VII.-Altes-Museum-Berlin1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
